BT 1 0 0 1 0 77.8 Tm .798875 Tw 12.4 TL /F5 9 Tf .058824 .090196 .164706 rg (Problem statement.) Tj /F3 9 Tf ( Routine ambient air quality surveillance relies heavily on physical Continuous Ambient Air Quality Monitoring Stations) Tj T* 0 Tw .504733 Tw (\(CAAQMS\). However, physical stations require substantial capital, continuous calibration, and grid infrastructure, which confines them almost) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.638733 Tw (exclusively to dense Tier-1 metropolitan centers. Regional air basins\227spanning pithead thermal power belts, remote non-ferrous smelters,) Tj T* 0 Tw .344071 Tw (mining corridors, and agricultural stubble plains\227remain severely unmonitored. This project implements an explainable, unsupervised machine) Tj T* 0 Tw .037333 Tw (learning workflow that ingests multi-sensor satellite Earth observation \(EO\) column retrievals, groups high-dimensional atmospheric vectors into) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.238187 Tw (clinically and environmentally reviewable pollution hotspot archetypes, and assesses how well these patterns align with airshed assimilative) Tj T* 0 Tw (capacity deficits.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 44 347 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 65.4 Tm 1.098125 Tw 12.4 TL /F5 9 Tf .058824 .090196 .164706 rg (Motivation.) Tj /F3 9 Tf ( The World Health Organization \(WHO\) estimates that ambient air pollution causes approximately 4.2 million premature deaths) Tj T* 0 Tw .5491 Tw (globally each year, with South Asia bearing the highest disease burden [1]. Fine particulate matter \(PM) Tj /F3 7.2 Tf -4.5 Ts (2.5) Tj /F3 9 Tf 0 Ts (\), nitrogen dioxide \(NO) Tj /F3 7.2 Tf -4.5 Ts (2) Tj /F3 9 Tf 0 Ts (\), and sulfur) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.661929 Tw (dioxide \(SO) Tj /F3 7.2 Tf -4.5 Ts (2) Tj /F3 9 Tf 0 Ts (\) exacerbate chronic obstructive pulmonary disease \(COPD\), cardiovascular ischemia, and acute pediatric respiratory distress.) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.504176 Tw (Sparse ground sensor networks create large 'geographic blind spots' where millions of inhabitants reside in high-emission airsheds without) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.5965 Tw (statutory air quality advisories. Fusing multi-sensor satellite observations enables synoptic, daily spatial coverage to identify and prioritize) Tj T* 0 Tw (mitigation across critical emission zones.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 44 266.6 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 65.4 Tm .034 Tw 12.4 TL /F5 9 Tf .058824 .090196 .164706 rg (Research gap.) Tj /F3 9 Tf ( Recent studies frequently apply supervised machine learning models \(Random Forest, XGBoost, deep neural networks\) to predict) Tj T* 0 Tw .372133 Tw (local ground station concentrations from meteorological inputs [3]\226[17]. However, supervised methods inherently require labelled ground truth,) Tj T* 0 Tw .034438 Tw (restricting their operational utility to locations that already possess monitoring stations. Furthermore, standard Euclidean distance metrics applied) Tj T* 0 Tw .566 Tw (directly to skewed satellite trace gas columns without log-stabilization distort cluster centroids. An end-to-end, unsupervised grouping pipeline) Tj T* 0 Tw .535625 Tw (that combines physical diagnostic ratios, robust scaling, external ground-truth validation, and carrying-capacity deficit auditing remains a vital,) Tj T* 0 Tw (unaddressed research gap.) Tj T* ET
Q
