BT 1 0 0 1 0 65.4 Tm .330875 Tw 12.4 TL /F5 9 Tf .058824 .090196 .164706 rg (Theme 1 - Satellite Earth observation and atmospheric column retrievals.) Tj /F3 9 Tf ( The launch of Copernicus Sentinel-5P TROPOMI revolutionized) Tj T* 0 Tw .29845 Tw (satellite air quality surveillance by delivering high-resolution \(3.5 \327 5.5 km\262\) tropospheric column densities of NO) Tj /F3 7.2 Tf -4.5 Ts (2) Tj /F3 9 Tf 0 Ts (, SO) Tj /F3 7.2 Tf -4.5 Ts (2) Tj /F3 9 Tf 0 Ts (, CO, HCHO, and CH) Tj /F3 7.2 Tf -4.5 Ts (4) Tj /F3 9 Tf 0 Ts  T* 0 Tw 1.295158 Tw ([1]. Veefkind et al. \(2012\) [1] and McLinden et al. \(2020\) [6] established that TROPOMI columns accurately detect localized point-source) Tj T* 0 Tw .564095 Tw (emitters and heavy industrial corridors. Remer et al. \(2005\) [2] demonstrated that MODIS Aerosol Optical Depth \(AOD at 550nm\) serves as a) Tj T* 0 Tw .475 Tw (robust optical proxy for columnar aerosol loading, while thermal anomalies from VIIRS capture active biomass combustion. However, satellite) Tj T* 0 Tw (retrievals represent integrated vertical columns rather than surface concentrations, necessitating meteorological dispersion context.) Tj T* ET
Q
